How to create variables in JS and execution details

Javascript follow hoisting, mean we can call or print variables even before declaring it 
for 
Ex: console.log(address); 
var address; -> is possible in VS which will give error in Java.
Because of hoisting. What does that means actually 


Order of execution of JS code
1. In Call stack -> Global Execution Context will be created

2. Global Execution context has 2 major parts
A. Method Context B. Code Context

3. Method Context: Holds or allocate the variable names and default values in key & value format, so hoisting means Jscrip will start looking from 
bottom how many and what all variables are created in program and allocate memory in Method Context area. Initially assign undefined value to it. 
key       | value
_______________________
address   | undefined

4. Code context: When pointer comes to line where varaibale is declare & define EX: var address ="Bangalore"
from here it will pick the value of varaibale address Bangalore & put in code context area. It will also update the value in Method context area 
from undefined to Bangalore. 

3. So if we are printing variable before declaring & defining, this is allowed because default value assigned is undefined & printed same on 
console
In Memory
